{"projects":[{"id":"superstore","title":"Superstore · Economic Performance","tag":"DATA ANALYSIS","tools":"R · Shiny · tidyverse · Plotly · Tableau","text":"Connecting retail performance with the economic context behind it.","details":"I combined Superstore sales with state GDP, population and income in R Shiny, then built a Tableau dashboard for regional sales, profit margins, monthly trends and product profitability. The full report, charts, R code and downloadable Tableau workbook are in the project repository.","source":"ETW2001 / Assignment 2","code":"sales.groupby(\"Region\")[\"Sales\"].sum()","kind":"dashboard"},{"id":"campus","title":"Campus Exploration & Rewards","tag":"ALGORITHMS","tools":"Python · Graphs · BST · Max Heap","text":"Exploring a campus through connections, constraints and rewards.","details":"Modelled locations and weighted connections, implemented greedy exploration, recursive path and reward calculations, and Top-K reward retrieval. The inspected implementation uses local difficulty choices and longest-path recursion; it does not establish a global shortest-path algorithm.","source":"FIT1008 / A2 Monash Survival","code":"campus.explore(strategy=\"greedy\", stamina=8)","kind":"graph"},{"id":"bigrig","title":"BigRig Mover","tag":"DATABASES / VOLUNTEERING","tools":"Oracle SQL · MongoDB · JSON","text":"Turning transport operations into connected, queryable data.","details":"Database work on customer quotes, jobs, employees and transport resources. SQL work includes joins, aggregation, subqueries, data modification and integrity constraints; JSON and MongoDB extend the relational workflow. Volunteer-service context supplied by Shuqing; implementation files are also stored as FIT2094 coursework.","source":"FIT2094 / Assignments 1 & 2 · volunteer context","code":"operations.query([\"customers\", \"quotes\", \"jobs\"])","kind":"schema"},{"id":"roguelike","title":"Farm & Roguelike","tag":"SOFTWARE ENGINEERING","tools":"Java · OOP · SOLID · REST API"